      "writtenOn": "2022-09-28T04:07:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not a fan of this fixed value; if we want to change it in the production code, it will break older CTS so we\u0027d be stuck.\n\nIf you have a test for the notification, one way may be to first test the broken case, and wait up to e.g. 1~2min for the notification; while still checking that there\u0027s no Available in the first few seconds as you do today. Then wait for the same duration with a small delta for the portal case. This would also make it clear that in the portal case, the point of waiting is to compare the 2 cases.\n\nThis way we\u0027d have a bit more flexibility to update the timing in the 10secs~1-2min range.\n\nThis requires a change to test for notifications though.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2889,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 2889,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "856b8b9f491523597152d9ee3ba1f3bd32dd4214",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
